In the LaTeX distribution there are a bunch of files that describe how =
to
manually install LaTeX with a certain TeX implementation.

More exactly they describe how this was done some time ago. As pointed =
out
during beta of the new LaTeX release most of these files are no longer =
correct.

As such files are contributed and cover distributions we do not own, =
there is
no way for us to maintain them.

question is how useful there are these days anyway. However, before =
sending
them to /dev/null I thought I run this question on this list as I guess =
if at
all then this list will have people knowing (and perhaps even =
supporting)
still existing implementations.

So if you are the maintainer of any such distribution or otherwise feel =
you
can bring one or the other file up-to-date, please send me an updated
version. All others will be marked obsolete and removed some time in the
future

thanks
frank

